# Citation metadata for this repository, in Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository" button on the
# repository page, which produces BibTeX and APA for the visitor.
#
# TO FINISH: once the repository is archived on Zenodo, add the DOI under
# identifiers, and set version to the release tag.
#
# Zenodo reads this file (it has no .zenodo.json, which would take precedence),
# so these values become the metadata of the archived record.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these course materials, please cite them as follows."
title: "EEB 603 Reproducible Science: course materials"
abstract: >-
  Course materials for EEB 603 Reproducible Science at Boise State University:
  the syllabus, the schedule, seven chapters of tutorials on reproducible
  research with R, R Markdown and Git, the assessment rubrics, and the data and
  example projects the exercises are built on.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Buerki
    given-names: Sven
    affiliation: "Department of Biological Sciences, Boise State University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8299-6539"
# license names ONE licence because that is what a Zenodo record carries, and
# CC BY 4.0 is the right one for the work as a whole: the prose is the bulk of it.
# The code in this repository is licensed separately under the GNU Affero General
# Public License, version 3 or later. See LICENSE.md and the License section of
# README.md, which is the authoritative statement.
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/svenbuerki/EEB603_Reproducible_Science"
url: "https://svenbuerki.github.io/EEB603_Reproducible_Science/"
version: "Fall 2026"
keywords:
  - reproducible research
  - R Markdown
  - open science
  - data management
  - teaching materials
